== How Long to Keep Your Papers

Here is what the IRS says about tax records, and some general habits for the rest. This is information, not tax advice. Your situation may differ, so check with a tax professional.

#v(0.1in)
#table(
  columns: (1fr, 1.25fr),
  stroke: 0.5pt + luma(140),
  inset: (x: 6pt, y: 5.5pt),
  align: left + horizon,
  table.header(text(size: 0.8em, weight: "bold")[Document], text(size: 0.8em, weight: "bold")[How long]),
  text(size: 0.88em)[Tax returns and the records behind them (income, deductions, credits)], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: generally 3 years from the date you filed. Many people also keep the return itself longer.],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Records if you did not report income that was more than 25% of the gross income on your return], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: 6 years],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Records for a bad debt or worthless securities claim], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: 7 years],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Records if you never filed a return, or filed a fraudulent one], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: no end date. Keep them indefinitely.],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Employment tax records (for example, for a household employee)], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: at least 4 years after the tax is due or paid],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Records for a home or other property you own], text(size: 0.88em)[IRS: until the limitations period ends for the year you sell or dispose of it],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Monthly bills and receipts for small purchases], text(size: 0.88em)[General habit, not a rule: until paid and the next statement matches. Keep any that support a tax deduction as long as that return.],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Warranties and manuals], text(size: 0.88em)[General habit, not a rule: until the warranty ends or you no longer own the item. Keep the receipt with it.],
  text(size: 0.88em)[Insurance policies, loan papers, deeds, wills], text(size: 0.88em)[Ask the company or a professional. Many people keep these as long as they are in effect.],
)

#v(0.1in)
